        "source_excerpt": "# Kalam Research Brief: Mu'tazili vs Ash'ari Exam Tensions\n\nThis brief is a compact source-grounding card for storyworld generation, not a scholarly authority by itself. Use it to stimulate doctrine-aware exam questions and dramatic dilemmas, then keep validator/human review in the loop.\n\n## Core Contrast\n\nMu'tazili kalam tends to foreground divine unity, divine justice, rational moral responsibility, and human accountability. A common dramatic axis is that if God is just, human beings must be meaningfully responsible for their voluntary acts; otherwise punishment and reward become morally opaque.\n\nAsh'ari kalam tends to protect divine omnipotence and transcendence by stressing that God is the ultimate creator of events and causal efficacy.",
