        ],
        "source_excerpt": "Mu'tazili-inflected cases can ask whether a thief, soldier, judge, or ruler can be blameworthy if every human act is directly created by God.\n\nAsh'ari-inflected cases can ask whether created secondary causes have independent efficacy, or whether apparent causation is a pattern of divine creation. This gives strong storyworld choices around evidence, medicine, fire, famine, and legal responsibility.\n\n## Exam Question Patterns\n\n- Ask the student to decide whether divine justice requires human origination of voluntary acts.\n- Ask whether attributes such as speech, knowledge, power, and will are identical with essence, distinct from essence, or only safe when named without asking how.\n- Ask whether a written Qur'anic verse in evidence is created ink, created sound,",
